footfall: a dashboard over the Spencer Street pedestrian counter

The council has had sensors on both sides of the crossing since 2013 and we have
been pulling the numbers into a spreadsheet by hand every quarter. This reads the
file straight off disk and puts the busiest day and the last fortnight on one page.

Pages live one to a module under footfall/pages and are found at import, so adding
one is a new file and nothing else. I did it that way because the last dashboard I
worked on had a router and a nav list that every single feature had to edit, and by
the end nobody could take anything out of it.

check.py renders every page it finds and fails if one throws, so run it before you
save.
